WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.020
Gear 5 has broken the Anime world, twice&nbsp;
now. And even though it is already one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:09.120
of the most iconic transformations in anime&nbsp;
history there are still A TON of unanswered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:13.320
questions and mystery surrounding these&nbsp;
incredible powers. So today we are going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:19.020
to discuss everything we know about Gear 5&nbsp;
and Luffy’s mythical sun god nika Zoan fruit.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:24.240
Starting with how Luffy actually awakened this&nbsp;
legendary power. And wow, let me tell you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:29.987
it seems like Luffy unlocked it by straight&nbsp;
up dying. Because in episode one thousand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.987 --> 00:00:36.540
seventy when Kaido absolutely crushes Luffy, and&nbsp;
our straw hat captain is apparently dead. While&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:44.040
this part isn’t exactly clear, Kaido sure seems to&nbsp;
think Luffy has died and heads down on a rampage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.040 --> 00:01:50.520
inside the castle. Even Momonosuke claims&nbsp;
that Luffy’s voice is “gone”, and since Momo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:56.100
has the voice of all things we should be fairly&nbsp;
confident that Momo isn’t making things up here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:59.820
although there is another explanation for&nbsp;
this that we will discuss in just a moment.

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:08.040
Because then we get this legendary smile. And&nbsp;
with this, Joy Boy has returned. Which actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:14.220
means that Luffy has awakened his devil fruit and&nbsp;
unlocked the true powers of his devil fruit. Plus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:20.160
conveniently, the Five Elder Stars explain&nbsp;
to us that Luffy’s devil fruit is really not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:25.020
the Gomu Gomu no mi, but it is instead&nbsp;
the mythical Zoan Human-Human fruit:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:30.540
Model Sun God Nika. So before we get into&nbsp;
all the crazy changes this will make to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:35.580
the story later on, let’s explain what&nbsp;
these powers appear to allow him to do.

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:41.820
First, the Elder Stars go on to explain that the&nbsp;
first ability of this fruit is to turn the user's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:48.600
body into rubber so that part is consistent with&nbsp;
what we thought about Luffy’s fruit all along. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:53.220
that is only the beginning because we are then&nbsp;
told that when fighting the user is supposedly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:59.580
only limited by their imagination, which is the&nbsp;
most interesting part about Luffy’s new powers.

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:05.520
That’s because Luffy then reaches down into the&nbsp;
castle with an ENORMOUS fist and grabs the giant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:10.740
dragon Kaido like he is a child playing with&nbsp;
some little snake toy. And then we truly get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:15.660
to see these wild powers in action because Luffy&nbsp;
puffs up his muscles like a cartoon character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:20.520
swings Kaido around like a tornado, and&nbsp;
slams him back and forth as if Kaido&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:25.440
was light as a feather. So clearly&nbsp;
Luffy has gained an incredible power&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:30.960
boost since he is able to casually beat&nbsp;
down Kaido like we have never seen before.

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:37.680
Which brings us to his next broken ability,&nbsp;
which is actually something that is normal for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:42.240
Parameica devil fruit awakenings. Because in&nbsp;
this episode we also see Luffy literally grab&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:47.640
the rooftop and bend it up to block Kaido’s&nbsp;
blast breath. So what he is doing here is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:52.260
turning his environment into rubber, which&nbsp;
we have seen many times before with awakened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:56.460
Paramecia devil fruits like Doflamingo’s&nbsp;
strings and Katakuri’s mochi. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.460 --> 00:04:02.100
something unique about Luffy’s awakened powers&nbsp;
is that he can also seemingly turn other people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:06.240
into rubber. We see this when later on&nbsp;
when he blows up Kaido like a balloon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:11.880
stretches through Kaido’s eyeballs and body,&nbsp;
plus even more. So his awakening clearly allows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:18.720
him to turn both the environment and other people&nbsp;
into rubber, at least when he is touching them.

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:24.300
But perhaps the most broken of Luffy’s abilities,&nbsp;
and the one that most people think of with Gear 5,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:35.280
is Luffy’s new ability to make his imagination&nbsp;
a reality. And this is where this devil fruit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:41.040
truly becomes one of the most overpowered&nbsp;
abilities in the series. Because as we have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:46.800
already seen in this episode, Luffy can now&nbsp;
do things that seem impossible. Such as freely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:53.700
manipulating his size to become bigger and buffer.&nbsp;
We will also see later on that he can apparently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:58.740
create things out of thin air, like goggles.&nbsp;
But that’s just the start because Luffy’s new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:03.960
powers might also explain one of the biggest&nbsp;
mysteries about his powers ever since the time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:10.020
skip. Because back in fishman island, Luffy first&nbsp;
revealed that he somehow had fire powers when he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:17.400
defeated this Fishman with his Red Hawk attack.&nbsp;
Then even against Kaido, he used an even bigger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:24.540
Red Roc fire attack, which just completely blew&nbsp;
my mind in the anime. For years, many people would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:29.880
theorize that Luffy could use fire because of&nbsp;
super hot friction, but now we finally know that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:37.620
his fire abilities might have just been an early&nbsp;
example of Luffy using his awakened abilities.

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:44.760
And that might just be the start of Luffy’s&nbsp;
elemental abilities because Gear 5 has even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:50.760
allowed Luffy to grab lightning and throw it at&nbsp;
his opponents, so in the future, he might even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:57.960
be able to manipulate other elements or devil&nbsp;
fruit abilities with his absurd new powers.

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:06.120
However, there are some very important drawbacks&nbsp;
and limitations that we simply have to discuss,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:11.700
including one that might change Luffy forever.&nbsp;
But first, even though it is explained that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:17.760
Luffy is only limited by his imagination, it is&nbsp;
definitely not an unlimited power. For example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:24.000
he cannot just "imagine" that Kaido is defeated&nbsp;
and it will automatically happen. So it isn’t an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:30.900
instant win condition. Also, the Gear 5 powers&nbsp;
seem mostly contained to Luffy’s body or things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:36.960
that he is touching, so he cannot just snap his&nbsp;
fingers and change the world. At least not yet.

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:44.760
Which brings us to the fact that much like Luffy’s&nbsp;
earlier Gear transformations, when Luffy uses his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:51.120
awakened powers it seems to dramatically drain his&nbsp;
stamina and possibly even his lifespan. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:56.220
we even see him comment that he only has&nbsp;
a few minutes to use his powers and also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.220 --> 00:07:00.900
witness a terrifying transformation into&nbsp;
an old man during a break in the fighting.

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:05.700
But all of this is nothing compared to one other&nbsp;
potential danger of Luffy’s awakening. Because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:10.500
remember when we said that Luffy seemed to&nbsp;
die before he awakened his powers? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:14.940
one theory about Luffy’s awakening is that&nbsp;
he actually did die, and then the spirit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.940 --> 00:07:20.940
of his devil fruit somehow took over Luffy’s&nbsp;
body. There is some evidence to support this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:26.040
such as Luffy’s heartbeat clearly changing&nbsp;
and his uncontrollable laughter while using&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:31.560
the form. Even this giant elephant comments&nbsp;
that this is the first time they have heard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:37.140
Luffy's unique sounding heartbeat in 800&nbsp;
years, They even then make it absolutely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:45.240
clear that Joy Boy has returned. So while this&nbsp;
hasn’t been clearly explained even in the manga,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:51.660
it is possible that by dying Luffy somehow&nbsp;
allowed the spirit of Joy Boy to enter his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.660 --> 00:07:57.660
body and bring Luffy back to life. Which sounds&nbsp;
weird, but we have to also consider that devil&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.660 --> 00:08:03.600
fruits seem to have a will of their own, so the&nbsp;
spirit of Joy Boy may have been living in this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:10.200
devil fruit for all these years, just waiting&nbsp;
for the right person to awaken the abilities.

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:16.500
Now you may be asking why is this dangerous for&nbsp;
Luffy? Well, when we first see this transformation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:22.500
it is a bit scary to see Luffy laughing&nbsp;
uncontrollably like this. It seems that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:28.080
literally cannot stop, so we have to at least&nbsp;
consider the idea that Luffy's awakening has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:34.860
let some ancient spirit come in and alter his&nbsp;
personality. Which could be why Momo felt that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:40.020
Luffy's voice disappeared because it is possible&nbsp;
that his voice just completely changed once he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:46.380
unlocked Gear 5. And while this is unlikely, who&nbsp;
knows what could happen with these new abilities.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:51.540
Although one thing that we have been shown&nbsp;
throughout the series is that whenever Luffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:58.320
unlocks a new ability - such as Gear 2, 3, or&nbsp;
4 - at first Luffy has some serious drawbacks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.320 --> 00:09:03.780
like a time limit or turning into chibi Luffy,&nbsp;
but eventually he masters the powers and can use&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.780 --> 00:09:10.500
them without much limitations. So maybe the same&nbsp;
will happen with Gear 5 in the future, which could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:16.500
lead to even more new powers in the future, even&nbsp;
though this is likely his last major Gear Upgrade.

00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:21.240
Now before we get into all of the insane&nbsp;
foreshadowing and future importance of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:28.380
Gear 5 for the story, let’s discuss a brief&nbsp;
history of the actual devil fruit. Because we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:32.520
knew all the way back at the start of the&nbsp;
story that Shanks and his crew stole this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.520 --> 00:09:38.040
legendary devil fruit from a world government&nbsp;
ship. So the government had it at some point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:43.320
which always made me wonder why they had it in&nbsp;
the first place. Thankfully we've recently had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.320 --> 00:09:48.660
some more context about this from Who’s Who, who&nbsp;
was one of the CP9 agents on this ship. And since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.660 --> 00:09:53.400
this was CP9 with the devil fruit, it makes&nbsp;
me believe that they were sent on a specific&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:58.920
mission to retrieve the devil fruit. So it seems&nbsp;
like the government had been hunting the fruit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.920 --> 00:10:04.740
which was actually confirmed in this episode&nbsp;
when the Elder Stars told us that the world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.740 --> 00:10:10.740
government has been trying and failing to&nbsp;
acquire the fruit for Eight. Hundred. Years!

00:10:10.740 --> 00:10:16.260
Wow, imagine searching for something&nbsp;
for that long, having finally found it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:22.380
and then losing it when some pirates steal it from&nbsp;
your ship. However, then we have to ask why they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.380 --> 00:10:27.900
wanted it so badly, but I think we can clearly see&nbsp;
the answer to that question in this episode. Not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:33.660
only is it simply an insane power that apparently&nbsp;
hasn’t been awoken ever since the Void Century,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:38.760
but the government must also be worried about&nbsp;
some secret abilities that we don't yet know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.760 --> 00:10:44.220
about. Could it be possibly related to the One&nbsp;
Piece? We'll discuss more about that in a moment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:49.800
but the government were so scared of someone&nbsp;
unlocking its true powers that they even changed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:57.540
the fruit’s official name to the Gomu Gomu&nbsp;
no mi. But now that Luffy has awakened it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.540 --> 00:11:03.720
we are going to see exactly why they have&nbsp;
been trying to claim it for all these years.

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:09.360
However, not everyone seems to be thrilled with&nbsp;
Luffy’s new powers, especially the reveal that we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.360 --> 00:11:16.680
had his devil fruit wrong all this time. And while&nbsp;
it isn’t the most clearly foreshadowed twist in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.680 --> 00:11:23.760
One Piece, there are scenes that we can point to&nbsp;
that might have hinted at these legendary powers.

00:11:24.300 --> 00:11:29.952
Of course, it all begins with the very first image&nbsp;
we have of the newly awakened Joy Boy. And if you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.952 --> 00:11:35.160
are thinking that this image looks familiar that&nbsp;
would be because we have seen a very similar pose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:41.640
multiple times in the story. For example, it shows&nbsp;
up twice in both of the bonfire scenes in Skypiea.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:47.460
So clearly this pose was clearly established way&nbsp;
back in the story, and this is even more important&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.460 --> 00:11:53.460
when you consider the context of the Skypiea&nbsp;
arc. The entire point of this adventure was to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.460 --> 00:11:59.400
free the Skypiean people from the false god Enel,&nbsp;
and how does Luffy do this? Ultimately he wins&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:04.740
the final clash by breaking up the dark clouds&nbsp;
to allow the sun to shine down on the praying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:11.220
people below. And if that isn’t super important&nbsp;
foreshadowing for Luffy being the literal Sun God,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.220 --> 00:12:17.760
then I don’t know what is. Besides, the concept of&nbsp;
the Dawn is a HUGE symbolic device in One Piece,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:22.920
and Luffy’s victories are often paralleled&nbsp;
with the sun literally rising like in Thriller&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:28.140
Bark or a dark period in an island’s history&nbsp;
finally ending like in Alabasta and Dressrosa.

00:12:28.140 --> 00:12:33.900
Plus, we’ve already mentioned Luffy’s fire powers&nbsp;
being possible because of Gear 5, but there have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.900 --> 00:12:39.180
also been other examples of strange abilities that&nbsp;
may have foreshadowed that his powers were more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:39.180 --> 00:12:44.880
than simple rubber. For example, Luffy’s attack&nbsp;
"Culverin" allows him to bend his rubber multiple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.880 --> 00:12:51.780
times. Many opponents such as Doflamingo and even&nbsp;
Kaido have remarked that simple rubber shouldn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:51.780 --> 00:12:56.580
be able to do this, but now it was likely&nbsp;
because of Luffy’s true awakening all along.

00:12:59.100 --> 00:13:04.380
But that’s not the only bit of foreshadowing for&nbsp;
this ridiculous power up. In fact, way back during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:09.900
the Impel Down arc, Luffy is talking to these&nbsp;
random prisoners and they even go as far as to say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:09.900 --> 00:13:15.780
that he must have been sent here BY DESTINY. Which&nbsp;
makes way more sense later on when we get the very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:15.780 --> 00:13:21.180
first mention of Sun God Nika in episode 1040&nbsp;
during Jinbe’s fight against Who’s Who. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:21.180 --> 00:13:26.820
this former member of CP9 was once imprisoned&nbsp;
in Impel Down and it was during his time in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:26.820 --> 00:13:33.060
prison that he learned prisoners sometimes pray&nbsp;
to the Sun God Nika who would supposedly free&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:40.080
slaves. This adds some much needed context to&nbsp;
the scene with Luffy talking to the prisoners.

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:47.280
Which brings us to the true purpose of Luffy’s&nbsp;
awakening. We’ve already discussed that the Sun&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.280 --> 00:13:52.080
God Nika is a legendary figure who freed&nbsp;
the slaves. It is very likely that this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:57.480
figure was also the original Joy Boy from the&nbsp;
Void Century since Zunesha told us that Joy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:57.480 --> 00:14:02.940
Boy had returned right when Luffy awakened his&nbsp;
fruit. And honestly, I don’t really think that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:08.580
Luffy is literally the old Joy Boy reincarnated.&nbsp;
Instead, it is more likely that Luffy has simply&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:08.580 --> 00:14:15.060
inherited his will and will continue to carry out&nbsp;
the task that the old Joy Boy never completed.

00:14:15.060 --> 00:14:23.460
So we have to ask, what is that task? Well, it&nbsp;
is the very same thing that Luffy has been doing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:28.260
all throughout the story. Freeing islands&nbsp;
and liberating oppressed people. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:28.260 --> 00:14:32.700
the only thing that we know for a fact&nbsp;
that the old Joy Boy truly wanted to do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:38.400
was some promise that he left on the poneglyph&nbsp;
on Fishman island. While we don’t know for sure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:38.400 --> 00:14:43.680
we can assume that this promise was to bring the&nbsp;
fishmen up to the surface where they could live&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:43.680 --> 00:14:48.960
in peace. So if Luffy is going to complete the&nbsp;
task that was unfinished by the previous Joy Boy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:48.960 --> 00:14:52.680
it will likely involve liberating&nbsp;
the world and all of the oppressed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:52.680 --> 00:14:57.180
races such as the fishmen, the&nbsp;
minks, dwarves, and other races.

00:14:57.180 --> 00:15:02.640
And Luffy’s return may have even been left in&nbsp;
a prophecy along with the legendary treasure on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:02.640 --> 00:15:08.340
Laugh Tale. That’s because when the Roger pirates&nbsp;
found the treasure, all they could do was Laugh&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:13.500
at what they found. The former pirate king even&nbsp;
states that he wished he could have lived in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:13.500 --> 00:15:18.600
time of Joy Boy, and he also knew that the One&nbsp;
Piece treasure somehow couldn’t be used until&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:24.420
twenty years into the future. But now that Luffy&nbsp;
has awakened we assume that the prophesized time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:24.420 --> 00:15:31.020
has come and Luffy will be able to use whatever&nbsp;
the first Joy Boy left behind on Laugh Tale.

00:15:31.020 --> 00:15:35.340
Which will ultimately result in a final&nbsp;
battle against either the Darkness fruit user,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:35.340 --> 00:15:39.420
Blackbeard, or the secret ruler of&nbsp;
the world government Imu. Either way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:39.420 --> 00:15:42.840
Luffy’s Gear 5 transformation is completely white,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:42.840 --> 00:15:47.460
which is the exact opposite of Blackbeard’s&nbsp;
darkness as well as Imu’s black outfit that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:51.600
we always see them wearing. And we have to&nbsp;
assume that because of the awesome powers of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:56.340
this fruit Luffy will surely come out on top&nbsp;
of this final world-changing clash and save&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:56.340 --> 00:16:03.060
the world. Which is exactly why the Nika fruit&nbsp;
made it into my Top 5 Devil fruits in one piece,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:09.420
and if you want to know which fruits are EVEN MORE&nbsp;
overpowered, you can watch this video right here.

00:16:09.420 --> 00:16:11.940
Shanks for watching and I’ll&nbsp;
see you in the next one.

